+                // .request() and py::object copy/move all touch Python
+                // refcounts. Upstream releases the GIL for the whole lambda
+                // via py::call_guard, and with pybind11 >= 2.13 (Python 3.13+
+                // opaque frames) the first inc_ref throws gilstate_error,
+                // which unwinds through the released-GIL frame and crashes
+                // the process (SIGSEGV/SIGABRT) -- this killed the learner
+                // after every self-play iteration. Acquire the GIL only around
+                // the pointer extraction, then release it for sampleData().
+                float *features_ptr, *action_features_ptr, *policy_ptr, *value_ptr, *reward_ptr, *loss_scale_ptr;
